==Icelandic==
{{Icelandic declension hk sb 01|haust}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|haust|lang=non}}. Compare Old English {{term|hærfest}}, English {{term|harvest}}, the Old High German {{term|Herbist}}; German {{term|Herbst}}, Danish {{term|høst|lang=da}} and Swedish {{term|höst|lang=sv}}.

The word {{term|haust|lang=is}} was originally masculine (as {{term|vetur||winter|lang=is}} and {{term|sumarr||summer|lang=is}}).

===Noun===
'''haust''' {{n}}

# [[autumn]], [[fall]]
#: ''Ég úrskrifaðist '''haustið''' 2007.''
#:: I graduated '''fall''' 2007.

====Derived terms====
* [[haustönn]]

